,"endPos":59095,"startLine":1061,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":1074,"endLineOffset":9,"length":902},{"pos":59105,"endPos":60008,"startLine":1076,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":1089,"endLineOffset":9,"length":904},{"pos":60018,"endPos":61327,"startLine":1091,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":1112,"endLineOffset":9,"length":1310}]}]},{"comment":"The logic in `nodeSettings` now checks if the node can contain data and whether it has either a `DATA_FROZEN_NODE_ROLE` or `DATA_ROLE`. This is correct but could be simplified for readability by using a method to check roles. Consider creating a utility method like `DiscoveryNode.hasDataOrFrozenRole(Settings settings)`.\nThe test `testCanMatchSkipsPartiallyMountedIndicesWhenFrozenNodesUnavailable` introduces several nodes and configurations, which is appropriate for testing the scenario described. However, ensure that all resources (nodes) are properly cleaned up after the test to avoid potential resource leaks or interference with other tests.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/searchable-snapshots/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/searchablesnapshots/SearchableSnapshotsCanMatchOnCoordinatorIntegTests.java-x-pack/plugin/searchable-snapshots/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/searchablesnapshots/SearchableSnapshotsCanMatchOnCoordinatorIntegTests.java-3947:3990,4086:4206,4395:4410-4293:4628,4724:4844,5033:5335","promptId":"#87X6D","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/searchable-snapshots/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/searchablesnapshots/SearchableSnapshotsCanMatchOnCoordinatorIntegTests.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/searchable-snapshots/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/searchablesnapshots/SearchableSnapshotsCanMatchOnCoordinatorIntegTests.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":3947,"endPos":3990,"startLine":79,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":79,"endLineOffset":55,"length":44},{"pos":4086,"endPos":4206,"startLine":82,"startLineOffset":16,"endLine":82,"endLineOffset":136,"length":121